I'd be ditching the GoPower in favor of leather (or dexterity if you
happen to have found them) and looking for jumping boots to replace
the speed boots.

> teleport control

Intrinsic?

> _What I dont have:_
>
> jumping boots

These are the only really nice thing on your list, but they're nicest
in the late game (Sanctum/Astral) so I'd keep an eye out for them.

> acid resistance
> disintegration resistance
> wands of death
> see invisible
> amulet of life saving

None of these are worth a wish.  Conflict is better than any of them,
but you can usually find it or polypile for it.

I'd wish for at least one more marker than the one you have--burn
those up writing ?enchant armor to get maxed out (remember that each
can be recharged once, and alot sufficient charges to write ?charging
so that you're able to do so).  If you're low on HP you might reverse
geno nurses  (in sokoban or a corner tower at the castle).

You can also use markers to rev-geno other things (tengu for intrinsic
telecontrol, wraiths for levels, etc), write magic mapping through
gehennom, identify if needed, ensure you have enough ?gold detection
for the endgame, charging for /death or lamps or whatever, etc.  I
might use a couple of your current wishes on them even with 2 in hand.

If Excalibur is the only artifact that's been generated, consider a co-
aligned artifact that grants MR so you can switch to a robe instead of
the CoMR.

After that I'd save them--emergency wishes are nice.  IF you get near
the end of the game and still have a couple wishes with a full kit,
then you can spend one on a luxury item (e.g. cursed potions of gain
level, a 'trice corpse, whatever) and still have another for
emergencies (the wrest charge is not a good emergency wish).

